.vscode/
.conda/
.continue/
.venv/
pyvenv.cfg
*.key
deployer_ssh_key
deployer_ssh_key.pub
gpg_private.key
gpg_public_key.gpg
cli/commands/__pycache__
# Generated trigger config is written to and read from
# `platform_config/{environment}/{team}/triggers/` — see decision 2 of
# docs/plans/finish-python-migration.md. Under `tekton_ci/triggers/` the only thing that belongs to
# the product is `templates/`, the generator's input; anything else there is output a previous
# version of kubementat wrote into the checkout, so it is not for committing.
tekton_ci/triggers/**
!tekton_ci/triggers/templates/
!tekton_ci/triggers/templates/**
platform_config/dev/smoke/
tekton_ci/pipeline-runs/smoke/
.aider*
*.egg-info/
# `.python-version` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the checkout's interpreter pin, and a clone
# that does not get it resolves whatever python the machine has (`requires-python` only says `>=3.9`),
# which changes the resolved click version and makes the suite report differently per machine —
# plan last-lap row 15. Removing this line is that fix; the file is tracked.

# Python artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
# `build/` is setuptools' own output directory, and it appears in the checkout because the E2E
# guest installs the local package through the read-write virtiofs share (`tests/e2e/harness/config.py`
# `GUEST_MOUNT`): the build runs in the guest and writes into the tree on the host. It is a build
# artifact and not a source change — `checkout-untouched` proves the tree is otherwise byte-identical,
# which is why this line is the fix rather than the assert being loosened.
build/
.pi/

# Local tooling state, never for committing
.codegraph/
.agent-work/
.claude/

.ruff_cache/
dist/
# Agent orchestration state (briefs, state files, reports). Tooling state, not product history.
.agent-work/
